4. The device table format
==========================

The device table is a line-oriented text file (one or more, via -devices=;
individual lines can also be injected with -line=). Blank lines and #
comment lines are ignored. There are four line types, recognised by prefix.

4.1 Device line
---------------

    <model>  <dev_id>  <host>  <opt1=val1,opt2=val2,...>

- <model> -- a registered model label (e.g. cisco-ios, generic).
- <dev_id> -- the unique device id. Must match ^[\w.-]+$ and must not be
  only dots. It is the directory name under the repository and the key in
  every status/lock/result structure. **A device id is never user-free-form:
  it is validated at load time.**
- <host> -- hostname or IP used to connect.
- the option list -- comma-separated key=value pairs. A value may be
  double-quoted to contain a comma or spaces (e.g. pass="a,b c"). A value
  of the form $TAG is a directory-allowlist tag, expanded for
  directory-valued options.

Example:

    cisco-ios  rtr01  10.0.0.1  user=backup,pass="s3cr3t",enable=en,repository=$REPO1,keep=30

4.2 default: line
-----------------

    default:  <model>  <opt1=val1,...>

Sets per-model default options. A device line of that model inherits these
unless it overrides them. Merging is per-option (device value wins). A bad
value inherited from a default: line (e.g. a non-numeric keep) rejects
every device that inherits it.

4.3 email: line
---------------

    email:  from=...,to=...,smtp=...,...

Configures the summary e-mail. If no email: line is present, no SMTP
connection is ever attempted. Options: from, to, smtp (host or
host:port), user, password, tls (off|starttls|ssl), report_dir,
write_report (on), email_max_diff, web_report_url, report_logo
(FILE|none), report_days, mask_secrets (off to disable), footer.
See README -> EMAIL NOTIFICATIONS for each.

4.4 directory: line (the allowlist)
-----------------------------------

    directory:  <type>  <$TAG|none>  [<abs-path>]

<type> is repository, template, fetch_run, report, or lock.
Presence of any directory: line turns the allowlist on; thereafter a
device's repository=, template_dir=, lock_dir=, and the on_fetch_run
program directory must resolve to an allowed path (directly or via a $TAG).
directory: fetch_run none / directory: report none disable that
capability. A directory: line that names a system directory, or is
otherwise malformed, is recorded in @dir_allow_errors and aborts the run
before any fetch. See README -> DIRECTORY ALLOWLIST for the full semantics
and --list-allowed-dirs for the linter.

4.5 Options available for all models
------------------------------------

debug, to, on_fetch_run, on_fetch_cat, timezone,
filename_append_suffix, comment, site, and the locking options (lock,
lock_dir, lock_retry, lock_retry_time) are available for every model.
Model-specific options (user, pass, enable, timeout, repository,
keep, fetch_timeout, changes_only, ...) vary by model -- see the per-model
options tables and the model sections in README (the DEVICE OPTIONS section).

